# Spark DS — Icons

## Source

Use icons from `assets/icons/` when a match exists (search, plus, trash, edit, copy, download, link, menu, dots, activity, circle-check, text).

## Implementation

- Prefer inline SVG React components or imports from a shared icons module in your app.
- Set `fill="currentColor"` (or `stroke="currentColor"`) so icons inherit token-driven text color.
- Size icons with component tokens (e.g. `--semantic-button-icon-size-medium`), not fixed px in JSX.
- Pass `aria-hidden="true"` when the icon is decorative; the parent control must expose an accessible name.

## Button icons

- Leading icon: place icon before label in DOM (default).
- Trailing icon: keep icon before label in DOM; add `spark-btn-icon-end` class.
- Icon-only: add `spark-btn-icon-only` and required `aria-label`.

```tsx
<button type="button" className={cn('spark-btn', 'spark-btn-primary', 'spark-btn-medium', iconEnd && 'spark-btn-icon-end')}>
  <PlusIcon aria-hidden="true" />
  Add item
</button>
```

## Do not

- Import icon libraries (Lucide, Heroicons, Font Awesome) unless the project already standardizes on one **and** Spark has no equivalent.
- Use emoji or bitmap images for UI icons in product code.
